I think the reasoning above from @saad-ali is right. I traced the origin code is from here https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/commit/8903e8cd857a725cf43dfd6710bb740413105479. At that time both file and block will call MountDevice repeatedly without checking GetDeviceMountState from actual state.
Later there is a fix https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/commit/6060c57ba3a944bd133968fd669980c97af846c6 to check the state, but it only put for file volume, not the block. So I think we should do the same for block here.

@jsafrane WDYT?
